WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.550
What if math stopped feeling like a wall of symbols?

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:04.200
Meet Catalyst.

3
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.175
See the idea.

4
00:00:05.175 --> 00:00:05.825
Try it.

5
00:00:05.825 --> 00:00:06.800
Make it click.

6
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:11.894
Install Python, extract the offline ZIP, and open Start Catalyst on

7
00:00:11.894 --> 00:00:12.298
Windows.

8
00:00:12.298 --> 00:00:16.339
On Mac or Linux, run python three start dot py.

9
00:00:16.339 --> 00:00:19.167
Open the local address in your browser.

10
00:00:19.917 --> 00:00:23.223
Start with a placement check, or choose a course.

11
00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:26.530
Explore narrated lessons from counting to college mathematics, one

12
00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:28.000
idea at a time.

13
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.322
Watch, then try three problems right below.

14
00:00:31.322 --> 00:00:31.690
Stuck?

15
00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:36.100
See an example, reveal why a step works, or open the calculator.

16
00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.181
Now make it real.

17
00:00:38.181 --> 00:00:39.179
Change an orbit.

18
00:00:39.179 --> 00:00:40.509
Test a gear ratio.

19
00:00:40.509 --> 00:00:41.840
Train a tiny model.

20
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.167
Move the controls and see what your math actually does.

21
00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:49.414
Fresh independent checks earn stars on your skill tree.

22
00:00:49.414 --> 00:00:50.968
Your work saves automatically.

23
00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:53.300
Come back, review, and keep growing.

24
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.827
Free, open source, and yours to explore.

25
00:00:56.827 --> 00:00:58.413
Start with one idea.

26
00:00:58.413 --> 00:00:59.603
Build from there.

27
00:00:59.603 --> 00:01:00.000
Catalyst.
